  "id": "deconstruction",
  "term": "deconstruction",
  "definition": "In this developmental psychology context, deconstruction means critically taking apart an accepted concept to uncover the assumptions, historical ideas, and power relations built into it. Here, it refers to examining the concept of development to show how adult-centered and linear views can justify treating children as deficient rather than as active participants in the present.",
